# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00203 M3 and M4, with the third acceptance fixes: rebuilds ccy 3.99.10.1, ccy-teams and the
# ccy image (container 2.75.1; the first launch after it rebuilds the image once).
# `ccy-teams session add` and `remove` change a running ccy session's teams without a restart (a
# session started on no team relaunches once, by itself, on its first join); M4 adds `session
# role`, `move`, `list` and `repair`, the coordinator options, one change at a time per session
# and one seat allocation at a time per checkout (both locks under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ccy, out of
# every container's reach). A session launched on no team is started with
# crossSessionInbound: refuse, so a message on Claude Code's own inbox socket is dropped instead
# of held for review. Running sessions are unaffected until they are relaunched: relaunch every
# team session after.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00203 M3 and M4, the agent team bus kit's pingbus and agent-bus for cc --teams and LXC
# members on the host: the watcher follows a session's teams as the owner changes them, the
# membership notice and its hook fallback, `seat farewell`, `seat retire` waiting for the sync
# lock; and (M4) `agent-bus seat take` and `seat choose` refusing a seat a running session's
# desired membership names, under the checkout's allocation lock; the status line marks a team
# whose homeserver is down, as `<team>(down)`. No unit or firewall changes; homeservers are not
# restarted.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00203 acceptance, every milestone in turn. M2: two throwaway headless ccy sessions in
# ccy's tmux in this checkout (plain and --no-bus, idle, no turn sent), removed after; checks
# the read-only mount, its relabel by labels (Z asked, container_file_t at the container's own
# level; on a Permissive host it says enforcement was not exercised), the inert kit, inbound
# proved by what the plain session's claude was started with (its --settings say refuse, and no
# managed settings outrank them; Claude Code's own inbox socket is only reported), idle CPU, the
# image version and --no-bus. Needs ccy launched interactively here once (Quick Launch). M1: the
# helper tests, then a third throwaway plain session: the seat keeper is its only pingbus process
# and only lock holder. M3: two throwaway teams acc-m3a and acc-m3b and a throwaway headless
# session on acc-m3a: hot add of acc-m3b, the notice, a human message, hot remove with its
# goodbye, no backlog on re-add, an idempotent re-run; all removed after (the first-join
# relaunch of an interactive session is the owner's step M3 (g) in ACCEPTANCE.md). M4: two
# throwaway teams acc-m4a and acc-m4b and two throwaway headless sessions: re-role, move handing
# the coordinator role on, two changes at once (75), a stopped homeserver (it stops and starts
# acc-m4b's; the session's status line says acc-m4b(down)), a killed seat keeper repaired, a session killed mid-add; all removed after. Then
# the server robustness checks (ACCEPTANCE.md R1-R9), on a throwaway team acc-robust it removes:
# kills, ends and freezes its homeserver and times its return, shows a stale backup on the
# board, times seat check waiting for a starting homeserver, checks any LXC member unit; its
# teardown also clears acc-robust's units from systemctl --failed and its backup timer's
# last-run time.
00203-teams-hot-control-and-robustness
# Plan 00201 M7 acceptance again: two throwaway teams, ccy --teams on both, then all removed.
# M3 now runs the status line the session's claude was started with, in claude's own
# environment, instead of a bare pingbus status-line from podman exec (which lacked the
# PINGBUS_HOME that pingbus seat exec gives claude, and so said the membership was unreadable).
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker/acceptance.bash
# Plan 00161 acceptance again (U20's seated headless sessions, then M2.11's named session).
# M2.3's idle turn no longer forbids every command, so the session can follow its rule 3 and
# start pingbus wait when the hooks say the watcher could not be started.
00161-agent-team-bus-matrix/acceptance.bash
